draw((4,-1)--(6,-1));
draw((6,1)--(8,1));
[/asy]

In this case, we can draw $2n-3$ tangent segments. We can prove this by induction on $n$. For $n=1$, there are no tangent segments, which is $2(1)-3$. Suppose that for $n$ circles, we can draw $2n-3$ tangent segments. When we add a new circle, we can draw two tangent segments from the new circle to the previous circles, and then we can draw a tangent segment from the new circle to one of the previous tangent segments, as shown here:

[asy]
